              ],
              "statement": "分部收入与营业利润包含基于相对价值、实际价格或成本加成等方法的分部间分配，以及基于相对毛利或相对员工人数的公司层面成本分配，因此不能视为独立经营实体的直接结果。",
              "citations": [
                {
                  "source_snapshot_id": "source-0019ae7ba0f6e3b63f944782",
                  "block_id": "block-001211-94df82c9",
                  "quote": "Revenue and costs are generally directly attributed to our segments. However, due to the integrated structure of our business, certain revenue recognized and costs incurred by one segment may benefit other segments. Revenue from certain contracts is allocated among the segments based on the relative value of the underlying products and services, which can include allocation based on actual prices charged, prices when sold separately, or estimated costs plus a profit margin. Cost of revenue is allocated in certain cases based on a relative revenue methodology. Operating expenses that are allocated primarily include those relating to marketing of products and services from which multiple segments benefit and are generally allocated based on relative gross margin."
                },
                {
                  "source_snapshot_id": "source-0019ae7ba0f6e3b63f944782",
                  "block_id": "block-001212-72e12aed",
                  "quote": "In addition, certain costs are incurred at a corporate level and allocated to our segments. These allocated costs generally include legal, including settlements and fines, information technology, human resources, finance, excise taxes, field selling, shared facilities services, customer service and support, and severance incurred as part of a corporate program. Each allocation is measured differently based on the specific facts and circumstances of the costs being allocated and is generally based on relative gross margin or relative headcount."
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
